   "source": [
    "# Syntergic Theory Simulation\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook visualizes the core concepts of Dr. Jacobo Grinberg's Syntergic Theory:\n",
    "- **The Lattice**: The underlying pre-space matrix of information.\n",
    "- **The Neuronal Field**: The operator generated by the agent's brain.\n",
    "- **Perceptual Reality**: The interference pattern resulting from their interaction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.abspath('../src'))\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from lattice import Lattice\n",
    "from agent import NeuronalField\n",
    "from transformation import PerceptualSieve\n",
    "from multi_agent import Swarm  # Import Swarm here\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set random seed for reproducibility\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Initialize the Holographic Lattice\n",
    "The Lattice is modeled as a high-density matrix of complex information (phase and amplitude)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 600x500 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "SIZE = 100\n",
    "lattice = Lattice(size=SIZE, dimensions=2, initial_density=0.1) # Added initial_density\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Static Snapshots (Optional, if we want to see initial CA state) ---\n",
    "# L_state = lattice.get_state()\n",
    "# plt.figure(figsize=(6, 5))\n",
    "# plt.title(\"The Lattice (Initial CA State)\")\n",
    "# plt.imshow(np.abs(L_state), cmap=\'Greys\') # Use Greys for binary CA\n",
    "# plt.colorbar()\n",
    "# plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "agent_low_coh = NeuronalField(coherence=0.1, frequency=5.0, size=SIZE, dimensions=2)\n",
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Low Coherence Agent (Standard Reality)\n",
    "An agent with low internal coherence (sigma -> 0) creates a noisy, distorted Neuronal Field. The resulting Perceived Reality is highly filtered and rigid."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x500 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "agent_low_coh = NeuronalField(coherence=0.1, frequency=5.0, size=SIZE, dimensions=2)\n",
    "Fn_low = agent_low_coh.get_operator()\n",
    "\n",
    "reality_low = PerceptualSieve.generate_reality(lattice, agent_low_coh)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Neuronal Field (Low Coherence)\")\n",
    "im0 = axes[0].imshow(np.abs(Fn_low), cmap='viridis')\n",
    "fig.colorbar(im0, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Perceived Reality (High Distortion)\")\n",
    "im1 = axes[1].imshow(reality_low, cmap='plasma')\n",
    "fig.colorbar(im1, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. High Coherence Agent (Shamanic State / Transferred Potential)\n",
    "An agent with high internal coherence (sigma -> 1) creates a highly symmetrical, unified Neuronal Field. The resulting Perceived Reality approaches the pure state of the Lattice, with minimal distortion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x500 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "agent_high_coh = NeuronalField(coherence=0.95, frequency=5.0, size=SIZE, dimensions=2)\n",
    "Fn_high = agent_high_coh.get_operator()\n",
    "\n",
    "reality_high = PerceptualSieve.generate_reality(lattice, agent_high_coh)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Neuronal Field (High Coherence)\")\n",
    "im0 = axes[0].imshow(np.abs(Fn_high), cmap='viridis')\n",
    "fig.colorbar(im0, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Perceived Reality (Low Distortion)\")\n",
    "im1 = axes[1].imshow(reality_high, cmap='plasma')\n",
    "fig.colorbar(im1, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 2: Dynamic Multi-Agent Resonance Chaining\n",
    "This section simulates how simple, low-coherence units of consciousness (Proto-Agents) interact over time.\n",
    "As they drift through the lattice, agents that are in close proximity and share similar frequencies will entangle, merge, and increase their overall coherence. Watch how chaotic noise self-organizes into highly structured, amoeba-like macro-agents."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x500 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Simulation finished. 100 initial proto-agents merged into 2 macro-agents.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from multi_agent import Swarm\n",
    "from transformation import PerceptualSieve\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, clear_output\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "NUM_STEPS = 50 # Reduced for quicker visualization of CA evolution\n",
    "swarm = Swarm(num_agents=100, size=SIZE, dimensions=2) # Reduced num_agents for performance\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run the simulation\n",
    "for step in range(NUM_STEPS):\n",
    "    # Calculate current state\n",
    "    swarm_op = swarm.get_operator()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # We'll use a hack to pass the global operator to PerceptualSieve\n",
    "    # by wrapping it in a dummy class\n",
    "    class DummyField:\n",
    "        def get_operator(self): return swarm_op\n",
    "        \n",
    "    reality = PerceptualSieve.generate_reality(lattice, DummyField())\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Plot\n",
    "    clear_output(wait=True)\n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    axes[0].set_title(f\"Swarm Field (Step {step})\")\n",
    "    im0 = axes[0].imshow(np.abs(swarm_op), cmap='viridis')\n",
    "    fig.colorbar(im0, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    axes[1].set_title(f\"Perceived Reality (Step {step})\")\n",
    "    im1 = axes[1].imshow(reality, cmap='plasma')\n",
    "    fig.colorbar(im1, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Advance physics\n",
    "    swarm.step(proximity_threshold=3.0, freq_tolerance=0.5, drift_speed=2.0)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Small pause for animation effect\n",
    "    time.sleep(0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "active = sum(1 for a in swarm.agents if a.active)\n",
    "print(f\"Simulation finished. 100 initial proto-agents merged into {active} macro-agents.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
